# the structural statement the numbers are pointing at
  An absorbing endpoint is sound exactly while the computation STAYS at it.
  The instant an operation moves off the endpoint into the interior, the
  interior datum's point denotation is asserted, and it is false, because the
  information that was absorbed cannot be recovered.

  So 'the top absorbs' is not a denotation for the numeral. It is a denotation
  for the numeral RESTRICTED to operations that cannot decrease, and the
  restriction is the part nobody has written down.
